    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive engine is anchored by the dual-threat speed of **Corbin Carroll** (79.02) and the power-park profile of **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91). **Corbin Carroll** remains a must-start despite facing a high-percentage hold pitcher in Holmes; his elite sprint speed and favorable dynamic platoon split against a righty starter provide the highest efficiency score in the lineup. **Tyler Soderstrom** receives a massive 16% park adjustment today, propelling his value against Baz, while **Josh Naylor** (71.44) rounds out our top-tier plays by capitalizing on a plus-matchup against Kay, bolstered by a helpful wind blowing out. While **Mickey Moniak** (66.49) is facing a difficult test against Nola, his dynamic platoon edge and order placement keep him as our most reliable streaming option for today\u2019s slate.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Austin Riley** (49.30) on the bench. While his pedigree is unquestioned, he currently sits below our threshold due to a tough matchup against Blake Snell, whose profile effectively neutralizes **Austin Riley**\u2019s base projection. He was the final cut over **Alex Freeland**, who maintains a higher ceiling today thanks to the favorable SP_xERA matchup against Strider. We are also monitoring the lineup status of both **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**; as they are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" their scores are tentative. Meanwhile, we have actively benched **Travis Bazzana** (38.72) not only due to a low efficiency score but also because of a 45% rain risk that threatens to truncate his plate appearances. With **Jose Caballero**, **Brice Turang**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Cole Young**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **James Wood** all providing stable mid-to-high 50s output, we are well-positioned to maximize our daily game caps without overextending.",
